  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 135 PM MDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nWe will be on a dry and warming trend through the rest of the\nlong term as flow aloft laxes and moisture decreases. While most \nof the upper level disturbances stay west and north, there may \nbe enough lingering monsoonal moisture to keep a few PM showers \nand thunderstorms going. Widespread rain is not expected given \nthe dry near surface conditions. Minimum afternoon RH values in \nthe mid to low 20s and gusty winds could promote elevated fire \nconditions, mainly in the northern and western counties. This \ndrying pattern is on track to be reinforced in the very \nlong term as the ridge builds back west and the jetstream stays\nout of our area.",
